      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is incredibly draining when therapy doesn't seem to instantly change the external chaos around you. When the environment itself feels overwhelming, finding small pockets of self-space becomes vital for survival. Can you identify just one tiny thing you can do or refuse to do for yourself each day, even if it's five minutes of silence? Focusing on microscopic moments of peace can sometimes offer a small anchor in the storm until larger changes can be made.",
      "source": "target",
